From ff2bb7bd7dfe2dcb407b66c80ed7b047e0ae7354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carl <admin@rtl-sdr.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:35:37 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] R820T: IF centre 1.815 MHz at ~2.08-2.6 MS/s (was 1.6),
 RTLSDR_R82XX_IF_1815

At 1.6 MHz a 2.4 MS/s stream (IF 0.4-2.8 MHz, spectrum inverted) reaches
below the tuner's IF high-pass corner (-3 dB at IF 0.47-0.51 MHz, chip to
chip): the top ~100 kHz of the band falls off steeply after a +1-1.6 dB
peak, the dongles' levels there differ by 2-2.5 dB and their phases by
5-10 deg. At 1.815 MHz (stock osmocom's IF centre for this bandwidth) the
stream is IF 0.615-3.015 MHz, clear of the high-pass; the wide-open
low-pass (FILT_CODE 0, 359a94d) is still above it.

Measured on a KrakenSDR (5 x R820T), 100 and 868 MHz, noise source:
phase between channels within +-0.4 fs 7.5 -> 4.3 deg (868 MHz: 9.4 ->
3.6) without equalization, the level at +0.47 fs -7.4 -> -4.0 dB, the
level spread between dongles at +0.45 fs 2.5 -> 0.3 dB. Only the 2.2 MHz
row changes (bandwidth requests ~2.08-2.6 MHz); the other rows keep
their IF centres.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/rtl-sdr.h |  8 ++++++++
 src/tuner_r82xx.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/rtl-sdr.h b/include/rtl-sdr.h
index 69ee037..1cbc2de 100755
--- a/include/rtl-sdr.h
+++ b/include/rtl-sdr.h
@@ -297,6 +297,14 @@ RTLSDR_API int rtlsdr_set_center_freq_gain_fast(rtlsdr_dev_t *dev, uint32_t freq
  */
 #define RTLSDR_NO_STREAM_SLIP 1
 
+/*
+ * Defined when an R820T / R828D tuner streams with its IF centre at
+ * 1.815 MHz for sample rates of about 2.08-2.6 MS/s (the 2.2 MHz filter row;
+ * was 1.6 MHz): the band then clears the tuner's IF high-pass, so both band
+ * edges roll off alike and the dongles match there in level and phase.
+ */
+#define RTLSDR_R82XX_IF_1815 1
+
 /*!
  * Set harmonic reception - for R820T/2 tuner
  *
diff --git a/src/tuner_r82xx.c b/src/tuner_r82xx.c
index d1977f2..a17935a 100644
--- a/src/tuner_r82xx.c
+++ b/src/tuner_r82xx.c
@@ -2050,7 +2050,17 @@ static const struct IFinfo IFi[] = {
 
 	{ 3, 1950+3,      1500,  30, 0x0F, 0x8F, 0x60 },
 
-	{ 3, 2200+0,      1600,   0, 0x0F, 0x8F, 0x00 },
+	/* IF centre 1.815 MHz (was 1.6, RTLSDR_R82XX_IF_1815): at 1.6 MHz a 2.4 MS/s
+	 * stream (IF 0.4-2.8 MHz; the spectrum is inverted, baseband +f at IF - f)
+	 * reached below the high-pass corner (-3 dB at IF 0.47-0.51 MHz, chip to
+	 * chip), so the top ~100 kHz of the band fell off steeply, after a +1-1.6 dB
+	 * peak, with the channels' levels 2-2.5 dB apart and their phases 5-10 deg
+	 * apart there. At 1.815 MHz (stock osmocom's IF centre) the stream is
+	 * IF 0.615-3.015 MHz: both band edges roll off alike (the RTL2832U's
+	 * decimation filter), the low-pass (FILT_CODE 0, corner > 3.7 MHz) still
+	 * clear. Measured on KrakenSDRs (heimdall_v2/docs/dev, librtlsdr-fork.md in
+	 * krakensdr_suite). */
+	{ 3, 2200+0,      1815,   0, 0x0F, 0x8F, 0x00 },
 	{ 3, 3000+0,      2000,   0, 0x04, 0x8F, 0x00 },
 	{ 3, 5000+0,      3570,   0, 0x0B, 0x6B, 0x00 }
 
